From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:58:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] milkflint tests: fake hardware for the KUnit tests

tests/fake.h: a sparse register file in place of MMIO, and a firmware
stand-in that records every MCU message the driver sends and answers it
with a reply the driver's parser accepts (optionally with a payload from
the test), plus mt76_test_dev(), an mt76_dev with both on a KUnit device.

mt7915/tests/fake.h: mt7915_test_dev(), an MT7986 probed the way its
platform driver does (mt7915_mmio_probe(), chip 0x7986), with the register
file under the driver's own address translation and replies going through
mt7915_mcu_parse_response().

First users: MAC_INIT_CTRL and its error path (mt7915-mcu), and the
MT7986's register address translation (new suite mt7915-mmio).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mmio.c            |   4 +
 mt7915/tests/fake.h      |  91 ++++++++++
 mt7915/tests/mcu-test.c  |  52 +++++-
 mt7915/tests/mmio-test.c |  62 +++++++
 tests/fake.h             | 365 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 571 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 mt7915/tests/fake.h
 create mode 100644 mt7915/tests/mmio-test.c
 create mode 100644 tests/fake.h

